@@name
ui-change
@@description
Make the user-interface change described in the user request, consistent with the existing components and styles.
@@requirements
    - Reuse existing components, tokens and styles instead of introducing new ones
    - The change works at mobile and desktop widths and with keyboard navigation
    - Text and controls keep accessible labels and sufficient contrast
@@approach
    Before editing, reason through:
    - Which component or stylesheet owns this part of the interface
    - Which other views share that component and could be affected
    Commit to the smallest change that achieves the requested result.
@@verification
    - Open the changed view in a browser at mobile and desktop viewport widths, take a screenshot of each, and confirm the layout matches the request
@@constraints
    - No new UI libraries or global style overrides unless the request asks for them
    - Other views that share the component must not change appearance
@@out-of-scope
    - Redesigning parts of the interface the request does not mention
